summary:
Integration of WP-A/B/C for the monitoring-act pacing redesign is done on the pacing-int worktree (HEAD 5fc0e06). The merged tree built and passed the smoke test with no breakage, so none of the WP-A/B/C interfaces needed changes.

**WP-A finished.** I ran feed-stages for all four channels and every stage. MEAN_SCALE now holds measured values instead of estimates. The biggest correction is CAM-01 stage 2: it measures 0.40, not the estimated 0.78.

Two legibility fixes, both checked in screenshots at CRT size:
- **CAM-03 trail:** invisible before. Its normals now mirror the far lamp (half-vector, roughness 0.3), so it reads as a wet glint at index 5–6. At index 4 his own body mostly hides it.
- **CAM-02 stage 1:** the heat glow now dims to 0.86 as well as gaining the smoke band. Before, s0 → s1 was nearly invisible.

**Pacing.** The node sim passes. The browser harness (?speed=4) gives:

| Persona | Act length | Longest gap | Cued alerts | Figure at end | Blind-spot violations | Errors | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| typical | 281.6 s | 18.4 s, in the 02:10 vent decay | 8 | 7 | 0 | 0 | PASS |
| eager | 253.2 s | 18.8 s | 8 | 7 | 0 | 0 | PASS |

The first typical run failed the gap check at 23.2 s. That was a harness artefact: the player was walking to the door, locking it and walking back. The harness and the ?pacelog summary now count lock-done and lever-done as events.

**Natural-flow contact sheet (960x540, 34 frames).** Every frame was read and all checks passed:
- the lock gate: prompt, 未鎖定 → 鎖定, SYS LOG line;
- every VMD cue: amber LED and the `▲ CAM-0n` line;
- the OSD tags, including `01:58:41`;
- each micro-event, and the CAM-03 paybacks (steps and sub-poses);
- the knock while he is still far away on CAM-03;
- 鋼板摸起來是溫的。 appended to the original-copy door text;
- CAM-04 frozen at 02:14:08;
- the SYS LOG merged in time order, all text in Traditional Chinese.

**Comfort.** Everything measured within limits:
- switching into darkened stages: CRT ≤ 14.2% per 0.25 s, whole frame ≤ 2.1%;
- the OSD alarm line: 5.9% on the CRT;
- the LED: 14.4% undulation over 2.4 s, steady under reduceFlicker;
- no new shader programs on the first view of any stage (89 → 89);
- whole act: peak −16.1 dBFS.

**Paths.** All passed with zero console errors:
- the loop reset unlocks the door and clears stages, alerts, frozen time and log lines, and the second loop's lock gate and first alert work;
- ?clock=02:08, ?lock=0 and ?pace=0;
- pausing during an alert and between the two knock sets freezes everything correctly;
- REVELATION/HD: alerts are off and the HD scenes line up with the LD anomalies.

**Residual comfort items from the fix pass:**
- **02:14 blackout:** the emergency-light transition is now 2.0 s instead of 1.5 s. The worst whole-frame change is 22.4% per 0.25 s (was 29–32%), still a monotonic 'power dies' drop.
- **Direct BLACKOUT entry (debug path):** fades in over 2.4 s. The worst change against the local level went from 52.5% to 18.8%.
- **Ending with reduceFlicker:** nothing flashes. The largest change is the scripted turn toward the dark door (26.7% against the local level) plus the near-black fade-out at the end.

I also fixed one real bug: the 20 s lock hint popped up while the wheel was already turning.

**Docs.** ARCHITECTURE, DESIGN-NOTES (new sections E and F, B3 changed to 02:05), README (debug-flag table and GitHub Pages note) and docs/pacing/STATUS.md are updated. The final build and smoke test pass 6/6, dist is restored and everything is committed.

